    "description": "Final assembly of the Operator record page.\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Tab structure: Details (Operator Details -> Management Details -> Billing Details -> Agreement) and More Info (All Additional Information + system fields).\n\n* Highlights panel is read-only. Any highlighted field that is also configurable must appear in an editable section below — Joyce: 'these have to also live down here. Like they're just like highlights from that lives below.' Same feedback she gave on the Deal page.\n\n* Rollup-driven highlights (Active Deals, Supported Verticals, Supported Markets) stay as placeholders until BUILD-148.\n\n* Working practice, learned the hard way on Aug 17: Lightning pages don't autosave and get buggy — 'save often. Don't make too many changes.' For a large change set, clone the page with a \\_V2 suffix from Object Manager -> Lightning Record Pages and build there, then activate. Kobi: 'I always like to clone the existing page and call it like version two and work off of the new one.'\n\n=== NOTES ===\n\n* ALREADY BUILT — confirmed on the Aug 17 Kobi/Taryn call. Ticket is retroactive documentation.\n\n* Build on the Dynamic Lightning record page using Dynamic Forms, not the classic page layout.\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Aug 17 call — assembled live\n\nDependencies: BUILD-126 to BUILD-134, BUILD-142\n\nOwner (proposed): Taryn Reithofer\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nCreated 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
